A committed key cell, focused
description: the key_cell_editing state
- >
  The entry's KEY as an editable cell - the caret ENTERS it (a click, or an arrow walk in visual
  order), the text edits in place. Reached by clicking a committed key or arrowing into it. Commit
  (Enter / blur) RENAMES the key: the server routes by STORAGE - a directory-backed member is
  renamed on disk (inbound `*` references and `&` bookmarks rewritten), an inline keyed entry has its key token
  rewritten in the body, value and comments kept (THE CONCRETE IS NOT A STATE). The rename is
  OPTIMISTIC - the key updates in place, the persist runs after any pending body edits flush.
  Enter then DESCENDS into the value's HEAD - the typing flow's own `k:` ⏎ landing, a fresh
  [entry hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole) at the first position - so a committed
  container stays enterable: its self value, a `&` bookmark, or a new first entry are one Enter
  away (a scalar's hole opens in its fields region at the self line; a POINTER holds no
  children, so the hole opens AFTER the entry - the sibling rule; a FLOW key walks to the value
  cell, flow has no block holes). A key that duplicates a sibling is rejected with the error
  ring, the typed text kept (keys are unique per node); an empty/unchanged key is a no-op. A
  DERIVED-anchor key (a positional dir-member's storage provenance) is not editable here
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', '', '`key_cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', 'the new key duplicates a sibling in the node', '[error_flash](*::server:yamlover-editor:error_flash)']
  - ['`enter`', 'a free (or unchanged) key, a block value - the rename persists (dir move or inline rewrite) and the caret DESCENDS into the value''s head hole', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`enter`', 'a pointer value - the rename persists, the hole opens AFTER the entry (the sibling rule)', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`enter`', 'a flow value - the rename persists, the caret walks onto the value cell', '[focus_next](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_next)']
  - ['`click_outside`', '', '`key_cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'caret at the start', '[focus_prev](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_prev)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '`key_cell_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`up_arrow`', '', '[focus_prev](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_prev)']
  - ['`down_arrow`', '', '[focus_next](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_next)']
